## Requirements

- [`helm`](https://helm.sh) - Refer to their [docs](https://helm.sh/docs) to get started.

## Usage

To use this chart add the repo as follows:

```sh
helm repo add pascaliske https://charts.pascaliske.dev
```

If you had already added this repo earlier, run `helm repo update` to retrieve the latest versions of the packages.

To install this chart simply run the following command:

```sh
helm install {{ template "chart.name" . }} pascaliske/{{ template "chart.name" . }}
```

To uninstall this chart simply run the following command:

```sh
helm delete {{ template "chart.name" . }}
```

## Metrics

The optional [Let's Encrypt Unbound exporter](https://github.com/letsencrypt/unbound_exporter) runs as a sidecar and exposes metrics on port `9167`. It is disabled by default. When enabled, the chart enables Unbound remote control on the pod's loopback interface and creates a ClusterIP Service for the metrics endpoint. The default image is community-packaged at [cyb3rjak3/unbound-exporter](https://hub.docker.com/r/cyb3rjak3/unbound-exporter); override `metricsExporter.image` to use another image built from the upstream exporter.

```yaml
metricsExporter:
  enabled: true
```

For Prometheus Operator, install its Custom Resource Definitions and enable the ServiceMonitor:

```yaml
metricsExporter:
  enabled: true
serviceMonitor:
  enabled: true
```

